77-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186279#post1186279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the funny moment when you understand that you could use the same concept for both a superhero and a slasher in the same time :P</div> </div> </div> </div>As with most Punisher-type concepts, To-mae-to, To-mah-to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:11:10-08:00","id":1186294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186289#post1186289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except he uses a shotgun and a bowie knife instead of traditional slasher weapons. I wonder how Malleus is gonna react to this guy?</div> </div> </div> </div>While many slashers do have iconic weapons, they are not exactly mandatory, so this can work.<br /> <br /> Would it be inappropriate if I tried my hand at writing ChroD versions of some of the Justice League members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:33:40-08:00","id":1186302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186294#post1186294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While many slashers do have iconic weapons, they are not exactly mandatory, so this can work.<br /> <br /> Would it be inappropriate if I tried my hand at writing ChroD versions of some of the Justice League members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, go ahead. Also, The Father would probably be a Avenger type of slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:49:04-08:00","id":1186306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186294#post1186294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While many slashers do have iconic weapons, they are not exactly mandatory, so this can work.<br /> <br /> Would it be inappropriate if I tried my hand at writing ChroD versions of some of the Justice League members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free. Though considering some of them are (overpowered) aliens, direct parrallels may be hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T09:02:32-08:00","id":1186328,"title":"","content":"I know this is mainly for heroes, but many classical enemies are mob bosses and the like, people who draw their power partly from influencing others: Kingpin and the Hand, Joker and his crew, Pinguin and the mob, even the likes of Bane and Ras-al-ghul rely on mooks. And what is a Hero without a Villain?<br /> For my Anakim Predator Mobster, I drew inspiration from such illustrious sources as Collossus, the T-1000, the Kingpin and Fullmetal Alchemist (mostly for the cheap joke of having a character named Alphonse with a Metal Golem Horror). Physically, I moddelled him after the great Ron Perlman in his role as Clay Morrow. What I think is often more true of Villians than heroes is the fact that heroes have two identities, while Villians quite often have just the one: they may have a (ridiculous) moniker, but they don't change their appearance by using a mask to do bad deeds. This is most often true for organized crime lords.<br /> <br /> Alphonse &quot;Iron Al&quot; Moran is an up-and-coming Mobster, been with the Irish Mob for ages as muscle, and when you do the dirty jobs and stay alive to reach his age, you're good at what you're doing. But after his awakening, he wants more, and is building up his reputation to take over the mob, then, the underworld, and after that... who knows, maybe the whole city?<br /> To achieve this, being an Anakim with traits like Giant, Looming Presence, Iron Skin+Iron Skin Advanced, Unbreakable and Relentless Hunter doesn't hurt. Throw in some Riot Gear, and there is little in the way of normal firepower that can stop this guy. Nightmares likes You're on Fire! (re-fluffed Bugs Everywhere!) and Your Rage Consumes you certainly help. The Anakim Birthright is always fun for a very unexpected ambush.<br /> However, so far, while climbing the ranks, this gangster has shown little to none guile - everything he does is achieved by brute strength. Indeed, when it comes to Manipulation, he is sup-bar, leaving him with unnecessary enemies and at a loss when a door cannot be pushed in by force.<br /> It's only a matter of time when he'll attract Heroes to his city...<br /> While he may have some redeeming qualities (Family-oriented and caring for his subordinates, honourable in so far that he keeps his word and has a code, etc.) he is still a criminal, unnecessarily violent brute, who hurts others simply for his own gain and for fun, and is willing to destroy any semblance of order and balance as long as he or his Family benefit from it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T09:10:22-08:00","id":1186332,"title":"","content":"I could see a Tamer of Fire becoming the inspirational leader/figurehead of a crime-fighting group in the vein of Captain America or Superman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T10:45:33-08:00","id":1186353,"title":"","content":"As far as Lyta Prince was concerned, her husband, Zeke, couldn't have died a minute too soon. She hated everything about the old buffoon. Well, almost everything. He may have been a disgusting, rude, lewd pig who could never touch her the way her past girlfriends had, but it was hard to hate his money. Especially now that it was all hers. And a lot of money it was. Enough, in fact, to buy herself an island, and to turn it into a refuge for all women who were as fed up with men as she was. Named &quot;Amazon Island&quot; after her childhood fascination with the legendary Greek warrior-women, the project was a big success, and even granted her a measure of international recognition at some point.<br /> <br /> Still, she wasn't content. Back when Zeke still lived, the thought of carrying and raising his child made her stomach churn, but now, she wanted a heiress of her own, a strong, bright girl who would carry on running her little utopia. Unfortunately, it turns out there are things all the money in the world can't buy. Deemed incurably infertile by world's best physicians, she turned to less orthodox methods. Over time, this grew into an obsession, and eventually, this obsession did bear fruit, though not quite the way Lyta imagined. In a fit of inspiration, she sculpted a perfect young woman from the clay of her beloved island, inscribed the names of the Greek gods on the statue, and prayed to them until the girl miraculously sprung to life. Lyta embraced her new &quot;daughter&quot; wholeheartedly, and named her Diana after the goddess of the hunt.<br /> <br /> Life wasn't exactly easy for young Diana Prince. For reasons neither Lyta nor her could fully understand, she couldn't really fit in with the women of the island despite her best efforts. And as Diana grew sad and apathetic over her alienation, it seemed the entire island fell into depression with her. It was perhaps for the best, then, that when the sea spat ou an unconscious man on the island shore, Diana grew interested in the world outside. Lyta happily funded her trip to the US - she even bought her a private jet! Although Lyta still misses her &quot;daughter&quot; and relishes catching glimpses of her accomplishments on the news, she hopes Diana doesn't plan to return any time soon...<br /> <br /> <b>Diana Prince<br /> <br /> Monster:</b> Promethean<br /> <b>Lineage: </b>Tammuz (Construct)<br /> <b>Refinement: </b>Ferrum<br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> Inscription (&quot;Hera, give me strength!&quot; - Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry)<br /> <b>Elpis:</b> Courage<br /> <b>Torment: </b>Naive<br /> <b>Role:</b> Soldier<br /> <br /> <b>Notes: </b>Diana came into existence as a fully formed Amazon warrior, with tons of Brawl and Weaponry. Now that she's into superheroics, she's probably stuck in the Soldier role to mitigate Disquiet. She doesn't quite understand how the world outside her home island works - hence the Naive Torment - but that doesn't mean she's foolish or slow, just culturally maladjusted. Should it come up, Tammuz Disquiet also plays into this - causing an incident due to miscommunication seems quite often for Wonder Woman.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:16:00-08:00","id":1186413,"title":"","content":"That is a great write-up Mo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:38:41-08:00","id":1186419,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I was actually surprised how well things map out. Though one thing about Wonder Woman I completely failed to address is her panoply - Prometheans don't really have anything that'd work for it, and i didn't want to stretch this already tall story even further by mixing in other splats' magic items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T17:08:15-08:00","id":1186481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186419#post1186419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I was actually surprised how well things map out. Though one thing about Wonder Woman I completely failed to address is her panoply - Prometheans don't really have anything that'd work for it, and i didn't want to stretch this already tall story even further by mixing in other splats' magic items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethan could use some magic items... it wouldn't be too hard to make items that grant access to or have the effect of certain Distillations.<br /> <br /> And Relics (as in Reliquary) are Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T05:04:36-08:00","id":1186617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186481#post1186481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethan could use some magic items... it wouldn't be too hard to make items that grant access to or have the effect of certain Distillations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely wouldn't hurt. Though I guess the reasoning for not doing that is that it would detract from the internal alchemy of Prometheans' own bodies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Relics (as in Reliquary) are Core. </div> </div> </div>Touche. I guess Diana's &quot;mother&quot; could acquire some while searching for ways to make a baby, and she sure wouldn't have sold them off on eBay when they turned out to be &quot;merely&quot; an invincible warrior's panoply <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The slight problem is, I haven't touched Reliquary in ages... I'll see what I can do about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:33:16-08:00","id":1186678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186279#post1186279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the funny moment when you understand that you could use the same concept for both a superhero and a slasher in the same time :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like how many superheroes would work well as Beasts. (Maybe Peter Parker's radioactive spider wasn't a physical spider)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186353#post1186353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Diana Prince<br /> <br /> Monster:</b> Promethean<br /> <b>Lineage: </b>Tammuz (Construct)<br /> <b>Refinement: </b>Ferrum<br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> Inscription (&quot;Hera, give me strength!&quot; - Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry)<br /> <b>Elpis:</b> Courage<br /> <b>Torment: </b>Naive<br /> <b>Role:</b> Soldier</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T01:18:32-08:00","id":1186981,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar582_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"582\" data-vbnamecard=\"582\">Morangias</a> that write-up is divine =D<br /> <br /> Now, we need some more of those.<br /> I'll try my hands at an idea stolen from the Superheroes thread:<br /> <br /> When Bruce parents were murdered, the boy was left inconsolable. A desire to take revenge took root, and he very quickly hatched a plan to strike fear into the hearts of men like his parents' murderer. He started working out, trained martial arts, studied forensic sciences... anything that would help him find and deal with criminal scum.<br /> Alas, a young man, even with his access to money, and his drive, could only get so far. Neglecting to protect his funds and shareholder majority in his father's company quickly cost him his main advantage, and neither his body nor his mind could keep up with the training regime he'd created. His martial arts training proved lacking when it turned out he couldn't effectively defend himself against multiple enemies and was beat up badly by two robbers.<br /> His goal was simply unachievable.<br /> But his desire to sacrifice had been noticed.<br /> A Man approached him, and made an offer Bruce couldn't refuse: funds, allies, skills, endurance, knowledge... all were his, for the low, low price of parts of his soul: a friend, an acquaintance, a relationship, a hobby: things that were distracting him from his mission, anyway.<br /> And so, Bruce Wayne reacquired his company with strategic precision, became wealthier than ever, mastered not one, but two martial arts in an extremely short amount of time, and with the help of a police comissionar became a vigilante that was to be taken seriously.<br /> From time to time, he would encounter new problems, enemies he couldn't defeat, and surely enough, the Man would appear again, offering him more martial ability, more raw power, more knowledge. He always left Bruce a more capable and more focused person. Soon enough, the mission was everything, his willingness to sacrifice increased and the only reason he acted as the civilian Bruce Wayne at all was to acquire more things the Man could ask for: friends, fiances, pets, experiences, vacations....<br /> <br /> Each time the Man took on the Cover of the Joker, the Penguin, Bane or the Riddler, he congratulated himself to the nice system he'd set up.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, less a write-up and more of a re-write, but I feel like this would be a very fitting place for Batman in the WoD if we're not going Beast =D<br /> <br /> Alternatively:<br /> When Bruce parents were murdered, the boy was left inconsolable. A desire to take revenge took root, and he very quickly hatched a plan to strike fear into the hearts of men like his parents' murderer. He started working out, trained martial arts, studied forensic sciences... anything that would help him find and deal with criminal scum.<br /> Alas, a young man, even with his access to money, and his drive, could only get so far. Neglecting to protect his funds and shareholder majority in his father's company quickly cost him his main advantage, and neither his body nor his mind could keep up with the training regime he'd created. His martial arts training proved lacking when it turned out he couldn't effectively defend himself against multiple enemies and was beat up badly by two robbers.<br /> His goal was simply unachievable.<br /> In addition, he kept having nightmares, until one day, he was Devoured by a Swam of Devil Bats. Ever since, he became a different person: he had a dark desire he had to satisfy, but at the same time, he was given the tools to exact the revenge he'd always dreamed of. And so, making use of his wealth, supernatural abilities and extraordinary focus, he took back the company, punishing those that betrayed him, and spread Terror among the criminals of Gotham City.<br /> Sure, the Batman could probably stop all criminal activity by using his extreme wealth and influence as Bruce to erect a system that would prevent criminality by introducing a fair chance, meaningful education and legal job opportunities to everyone, or kill those pesky buggers that keep escaping prison again and again - but then, how would he feed?<br /> <br /> This version of Batman makes use of a lot of abilities and skills rather than gadgets. Again, more of a re-write than a write-up.<br /> <br /> <b>Bruce Wayne<br /> <br /> Monster:</b> Beast<br /> <b>Family: </b>Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Punishment<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless<br /> <b>Life: </b>Protective<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Mimir's Wisdom, Relentless Hunter, From the Shadows, Shadowed Soul, Eye of Heaven, Needs Must, Wings of the Raptor, Looming Presence<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: Fear is Contagious, Everything you do is Worthless, Run Away<br /> <b>Merits</b>: several Fighting Styles 5, Alternate Identity 3, Epic Potential (Strength), Eidetic Memory (advanced), Direction Sense (advanced), Danger Sense (advanced), Fleet of Foot, Fast Reflexes (advanced), Good Time Management, Patient, Guilty Pleasure (Intimidating Kal-El), Hunger Management, Indomitable, Iron Skin (advanced), Iron Will, Parkour 5, Sleight of Hand, Trained Observer 3, and many more. It's the goddamn Batman!<br /> <b>Lair Traits: </b>Darkness, Exposed, Echoing, Sealed Exits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T23:37:31-08:00","id":1187473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1186981#post1186981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bruce Wayne<br /> <br /> Monster:</b> Beast<br /> <b>Family: </b>Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Punishment<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless<br /> <b>Life: </b>Protective</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, Bruce Wayne would be <i>Ugallu</i> - Bat-Man, is in the end, flying terror of SEEING things, looming from scycrapers and watching over the community. Bats are flying predators in the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T08:17:12-08:00","id":1187558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1187473#post1187473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, Bruce Wayne would be <i>Ugallu</i> - Bat-Man, is in the end, flying terror of SEEING things, looming from scycrapers and watching over the community. Bats are flying predators in the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say both are valid interpretations, depending on what aspects of Batman you consider the most important to his character. But personally, I prefer him as Ugallu as well.<br /> <br /> Now, to finish the Big Three:<br /> <br /> Sometimes, young Clark would joke that he feels like an alien from another planet. All too often, those who heard him would think he may be right. Among the young people of Smallville, the adopted son of Kents has always stood out, and in a good way. Tall and handsome, hale and strong, yet also smart, caring and honest, he gave most people a mild inferiority complex at best. Some resented him for it, others were in awe, but nobody truly understood him.<br /> <br /> Since early childhood, being the best, most perfect kid any parent would want was Clark\u2019s only option, as far as he was concerned. And it was neither due to Kents\u2019 upbringing nor the usual need of an orphan kid to prove himself, though these certainly played a part too. No, it was because, ever since Clark would remember, he would dream of a giant figure, its skin made of invulnerable steel, its face sculpted like that of a Greek god, floating in the void of space, solar disk at its back, watching the Earth ceaselessly with glowing red eyes. Watching Clark.<br /> <br /> Ma Kent would teach him about God, and how He would always watch over people, and to Clark, this always sounded as a distorted reflection of the truth he knew - someone was watching, after all. That he didn\u2019t look much like the smiling old man Ma Kent imagined\u2026 well, maybe it was better she didn\u2019t know all the details, after all. It was enough that Clark knew. Each night he contemplated the giant man in the sky, and each night he would get closer to understanding humanity. People, Clark realized, weren\u2019t inherently bad. They just didn\u2019t know better. They did bad things because they were tiny and afraid. If they knew, truly knew, that a superior being watches over them, Clark reasoned, they wouldn\u2019t act out of fear for their tiny lives. Instead, they could work on bettering themselves, so they could be more like the perfect giant themselves.<br /> <br /> One night, as Clark was nearing his eighteenth birthday, he dreamt of the giant again. But this time was different. As he looked up towards the figure, he felt a sudden rush of confidence, leapt off the face of the earth, and flew right up to the giant. There, in the blinding light of the sun, he could finally see the details of the giant\u2019s face, and realized he was looking at himself all along. Then, Clark knew his destiny. One day, he will show himself to the people of the world. Then, everybody will know safety under his benevolent gaze.<br /> <br /> <b>Clark Kent</b><br /> <br /> <b>Monster:</b> Beast<br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Judgmental<br /> <b>Life:</b> Selfless<br /> <b>Key Atavisms:</b> All Anakim, Unbreakable, Dragonfire (\u201cheat vision\u201d), Wings of the Raptor, Needs Must<br /> <b>Key Nightmares:</b> Everything You Do Is Worthless, Run Away, You Deserve This<br /> <b>Key Lair Traits:</b> Blazing Light, Exposed, everything wind- and cold-related (to emulate the freezing breath-and the environment of Fortress of Solitude).<br /> <b>Key traits: </b>Power and Resistance Attributes across all three categories (but primarily physical), Empathy, Athletics, Brawl, Craft Specialty: Super-Weaving, Larceny Specialties: Phone Booths, Ridiculously Thin Disguises.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> For all the raw power of a Beast (and an Anakim at that), this version of Supes is still more akin to his golden age incarnation, leaping tall buildings rather than truly flying over them. That said, the common story of Superman making himself known to humanity during some sort of crisis (be it a plane threatening to fall right on top of Metropolis or Doomsday/Darkseid/Zod/Whatever doing much the same) might be construed as a ploy to build a Myth and become an Incarnate, and the power that entails would bring him much closer to his graphic novel origins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T10:06:25-08:00","id":1187587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1185777-crossover-concept-vigilante-society?p=1187473#post1187473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, Bruce Wayne would be <i>Ugallu</i> - Bat-Man, is in the end, flying terror of SEEING things, looming from scycrapers and watching over the community. Bats are flying predators in the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that a viable interpretation, and feeling exposed certainly is a big part of most versions of Batman. Just as much as you could see that the main thing about Batman is that he is practically unstoppable and always wins, thus inducing a feeling of helplessness in a majority of his enemies (usually mooks, sometimes even major enemies), which would make him an Anakim.<br /> You could also make him a Makara, by virtue of him outdoing his enemies quite often through strategy, or from their point of view, being pulled from their favourite game into his game.<br /> I went with Eshmaki because imo the most striking thing about him is the Unseen Hunter schtick, even using that to play mindgames on people occasionally, and it fits into his usual modus operandi: dramatic entrance via surprise attack, hide in darkness to strike again, thus take out multiple opponents one by one without ever getting hit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}